From: GZ302 camera bring-up <local>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: enable the ISP GPIO for GZ302 camera capture

The AMD ISP4 capture driver requires an "enable_isp" GPIO descriptor before
it can register the V4L2 subdevice.  The reference board registers this
lookup table only for its OMNI5C10 sensor.  The GZ302's OMNI13B1 ACPI device
also has no GPIO resources, while its ISP power-enable line is provided by
the same AMDI0030 controller lookup used by the ISP4 reference platform.

Register the ISP enable lookup for the GZ302.  Do not register the OV05C10
sensor's separate GPIO lookup: OV13B10 does not request that "enable" GPIO.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/isp_v4_1_1.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/isp_v4_1_1.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/isp_v4_1_1.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/isp_v4_1_1.c
@@ -241,8 +241,11 @@
 	}
 
 	/* add GPIO resources required for OMNI5C10 sensor */
-	if (!strcmp("OMNI5C10", acpi_device_hid(acpi_dev))) {
+	if (!strcmp("OMNI5C10", acpi_device_hid(acpi_dev)) ||
+	    !strcmp("OMNI13B1", acpi_device_hid(acpi_dev)))
 		gpiod_add_lookup_table(&isp_gpio_table);
+
+	if (!strcmp("OMNI5C10", acpi_device_hid(acpi_dev))) {
 		gpiod_add_lookup_table(&isp_sensor_gpio_table);
 	}
 
